\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the proposed \text  {H-GNN} framework. Heterogeneous multi-architecture ELF binaries are lifted into architecture-agnostic VEX IR, decomposed into a two-level hierarchical graph (bounded intra-procedural CFGs and an inter-procedural call graph reconstructed from control-flow primitives), and encoded bottom-up with GATv2 and GraphSAGE for binary malware detection.}}{4}{figure.1.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_overview}{{1}{4}{Overview of the proposed \text {H-GNN} framework. Heterogeneous multi-architecture ELF binaries are lifted into architecture-agnostic VEX IR, decomposed into a two-level hierarchical graph (bounded intra-procedural CFGs and an inter-procedural call graph reconstructed from control-flow primitives), and encoded bottom-up with GATv2 and GraphSAGE for binary malware detection}{figure.1.1}{}}
